      "writtenOn": "2020-06-08T16:56:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be highly preferable to avoid not_native_bridge.  Can the necessary use cases be handled by patterns like:\n\n    native_bridge: {\n        exclude_srcs: [...],\n    },",
      "revId": "a4c17d47c625258decb97d3d30a18a2bc55bda24",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "26595e55_486f1784",
        "filename": "android/arch.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1030,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069991
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-08T17:06:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One of the necessary use cases is\n\nnot_native_bridge: {\n  enabled: false,\n},\n\nto make sure there are no conflict between stub libraries and original libraries.\n\nAnd then, in RenderScript itself:\n\nnot_native_bridge: {\n  shared_libs: [\n    \"libnativewindow\"\n  ],\n},\nnot_native_bridge: {\n  shared_libs: [\n    \"libndk_translation_guest_libnativewindow\"\n  ],\n},\n\nTo make sure it\u0027s build with library which would actually be used in runtime and we wouldn\u0027t need to build 100+ libraries which we don\u0027t intend to ever use.",
      "parentUuid": "b0ee2a96_77efc85e",
      "revId": "a4c17d47c625258decb97d3d30a18a2bc55bda24",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a47ff386_c9795ba8",
        "filename": "android/arch.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1030,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-08T18:36:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d suggest moving the enabled: false to either its own module type:\n\n    cc_native_bridge_library {\n        ...\n    }\n\nor to a bool on cc_library:\n\n    cc_library {\n        native_bridge_stubs: true,\n    }\n\nFor the shared_libs, I\u0027d suggest:\n\n    shared_libs: [\"libnativewindow\"],\n    native_bridge: {\n        exclude_shared_libs: [\"libnativewindow\"],\n        shared_libs: [\"libndk_translation_guest_libnativewindow\"],\n    },\n\nAlternatively, if you\u0027re willing to keep a global mapping of libraries to your stub libraries somewhere, and this pattern should apply to all module that depend on a library that has stubs, we could rewrite those dependencies automatically for the m.Target().NativeBridgeEnabled case.  We do that for e.g. VNDK libraries, where IIRC a dependency on \"libc\" gets rewritten to \"libc.vendor\".",
      "parentUuid": "26595e55_486f1784",
      "revId": "a4c17d47c625258decb97d3d30a18a2bc55bda24",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "658564f3_cd497b44",
        "filename": "android/arch.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1030,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069991
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-08T20:49:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually we could do the same with \"enabled\" as you suggest to do with shared_libs.\n\nIn fact that\u0027s already done more-or-less this way:\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/android/vendor/unbundled_google/libs/ndk_translation/native_bridge_support/Android.bp;rcl\u003d5efc200bbaa1ef77c0c2ca6f71f8243a346bd3b4;l\u003d43\n\nGlobal mapping looks a bit like an overkill at this point: we have dozens of libraries which are built as stubs and dozens as full libraries but only need a handful of libraries with these alternating dependencies.",
      "parentUuid": "a47ff386_c9795ba8",
      "revId": "a4c17d47c625258decb97d3d30a18a2bc55bda24",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
